Acknowledgements
================

The Tobii Eye Tracker 5 driver in crates/gaze-provider-et5 is a Rust implementation of a
protocol other people worked out first:

- tobiifree (https://github.com/Aetherall/tobiifree, GPL-3.0) documented the ET5's USB
  protocol: the TTP framing, the TLV payloads, the realm unlock and the gaze stream
  columns, along with the opcode map and blob framing in its issue #3. Two things in
  crates/gaze-provider-et5/src/ttp.rs come from its Zig driver
  (driver/src/tobiifree_core.zig): the 47-byte hello payload and the 20-byte subscribe
  template, taken verbatim, and the frame-builder and reassembly tests, translated from
  its tests with the same scenarios, inputs and expected values.
- nottobii (https://github.com/puffnfresh/nottobii, GPL-3.0) recorded the Windows
  driver's initialisation order from packet captures, which the connect sequence in
  device.rs follows.
- Talon's talon_plugins/eye_mouse.py (https://talonvoice.com) supplied the calibration
  opcode map and the round schedule the retrain ceremony is modelled on (small rounds
  with an apply after each, Talon's 1, 4 and 4 points over a 600x340 mm area), along
  with its gaze-vote acceptance gate.

The Daydream controller packet layout in crates/gaze-daydream follows mrdoob's reverse
engineering in daydream-controller.js (https://github.com/mrdoob/daydream-controller.js,
MIT).

Models (not distributed by this repository; see README.md)
-----------------------------------------------------------

- TargetFinder widget detector: "TargetFinder: Detecting Widgets from Pixels on Desktop
  Interfaces", arXiv:2607.19907. Code and checkpoints at
  https://github.com/ahmedbenakouche/target_finder_toolkit (MIT). The checkpoints are an
  Ultralytics YOLO26n fine-tune whose metadata says AGPL-3.0; the export is made locally
  by crates/gaze-detect/scripts/fetch_models.py, which runs Ultralytics (AGPL-3.0).
- PP-OCRv5 mobile text detector by PaddlePaddle (Apache-2.0), in the ONNX conversion
  published at https://huggingface.co/webnn/PP-OCRv5-ONNX.

